  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:ezekiel:15:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "And the word of the LORD came unto me, saying,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ezekiel 15:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ezekiel:15:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:ezekiel:15:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Son of man, What is the vine tree more than any tree, or than a branch which is among the trees of the forest?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ezekiel 15:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ezekiel:15:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:ezekiel:15:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Shall wood be taken thereof to do any work? or will men take a pin of it to hang any vessel thereon?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ezekiel 15:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ezekiel:15:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:ezekiel:15:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Behold, it is cast into the fire for fuel; the fire devoureth both the ends of it, and the midst of it is burned. Is it meet for any work?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ezekiel 15:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ezekiel:15:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:ezekiel:15:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Behold, when it was whole, it was meet for no work: how much less shall it be meet yet for any work, when the fire hath devoured it, and it is burned?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ezekiel 15:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ezekiel:15:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:ezekiel:15:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Therefore thus saith the Lord GOD; As the vine tree among the trees of the forest, which I have given to the fire for fuel, so will I give the inhabitants of Jerusalem.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ezekiel 15:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ezekiel:15:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:ezekiel:15:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "And I will set my face against them; they shall go out from one fire, and another fire shall devour them; and ye shall know that I am the LORD, when I set my face against them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ezekiel 15:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ezekiel:15:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:ezekiel:15:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "And I will make the land desolate, because they have committed a trespass, saith the Lord GOD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ezekiel 15:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ezekiel:15:8"
      }
    }
  ],
